From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NXP-MR <meta-nxp-mr@nxp.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Jul 2026 16:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dpuv2: Select DPU render node by driver name

dpuOpen() hard-codes DRM render node minor 128 (/dev/dri/renderD128).
DRM render node minors are assigned in driver registration order, so
this only works when the DPU is the first DRM driver to register a
render node.

On i.MX95 the DPU display controller is built into the kernel but
defers its probe during early boot (waiting on clocks/power). When the
Mesa/panthor graphics stack is used, the Mali GPU (panthor) is loaded
as a module by udev and registers its render node first, taking
renderD128 and pushing the DPU render node to renderD129. dpuOpen()
then opens the panthor node, the DPU version ioctl fails with

    ERROR: invalid version of dpu devices returned

and every g2d blit silently produces black output (breaking
imxvideoconvert_g2d, imxcompositor_g2d, etc.).

With the legacy proprietary Mali driver (mali_kbase) this did not
happen because that driver exposes a character device instead of a DRM
render node, so the DPU always ended up on renderD128.

Instead of assuming a fixed minor, scan the render nodes and pick the
one whose DRM driver name identifies the DPU. Fall back to the historic
fixed node if none matches.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: NXP-MR <meta-nxp-mr@nxp.com>
---
--- a/dpuv2/hardware/dpu_ioctl.c
+++ b/dpuv2/hardware/dpu_ioctl.c
@@ -77,10 +77,42 @@
 	int fd;
 
 #if defined(OPENDRMDEVICE)
-	int drm_minor = 128;
+	int drm_minor;
 
-	fd = drmOpenRender(drm_minor);
+	/*
+	 * The DPU 2D blit engine is exposed as a DRM render node. Its minor
+	 * number is assigned in DRM registration order and is therefore not
+	 * guaranteed to be 128: when another DRM driver (e.g. the Mali GPU
+	 * driver on i.MX95 when using the Mesa/panthor stack) registers a
+	 * render node first, the DPU node is pushed to a higher minor. Scan
+	 * the render nodes and pick the one whose DRM driver name identifies
+	 * the DPU instead of assuming render node 128.
+	 */
+	fd = -1;
+	for (drm_minor = 128; drm_minor < 128 + 16; drm_minor++) {
+		int candidate = drmOpenRender(drm_minor);
+		drmVersionPtr version;
 
+		if (candidate < 0)
+			continue;
+
+		version = drmGetVersion(candidate);
+		if (version != NULL) {
+			int is_dpu = (version->name != NULL) &&
+				     (strstr(version->name, "dpu") != NULL);
+
+			drmFreeVersion(version);
+			if (is_dpu) {
+				fd = candidate;
+				break;
+			}
+		}
+		drmClose(candidate);
+	}
+
+	/* Fall back to the historical fixed render node if none matched. */
+	if (fd < 0)
+		fd = drmOpenRender(128);
 
 #elif defined(EXTERN_IOCTL)
 	fd = open_handler(DPU_DEVICE_NAME, O_RDWR, 0);
-- 
